libsircl
Copyright 2026 SparkRing contributors

libsircl is SIRCL's NCCL-compatible C API, part of SparkRing's SIRCL ring sessions, licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE). It is an independent implementation of the NCCL C
interface. It is not NVIDIA NCCL and is not sponsored or endorsed by NVIDIA Corporation.

NCCL interface header
  include/nccl.h is a modified copy of src/nccl.h.in from NVIDIA NCCL at tag v2.32.3-1
  (https://github.com/NVIDIA/nccl), Copyright (c) 2015-2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The unmodified file and NCCL's LICENSE.txt are in
  vendor/. src/stubs.c, src/aliases.c and tests/api_manifest.json are generated from that header
  and reproduce its function declarations.

SIRCL components
  src/transport/sircl_roce_proxy.c, src/transport/sircl_p2p_proxy.c and
  src/transport/fake_verbs/infiniband/verbs.h are copies of SIRCL files. The kernels in
  kernels/sircl_kernels.cu, kernels/sircl_common.cuh, kernels/sircl_links.cu and kernels/sircl_p2p.cu
  are CUDA C++ ports of SIRCL's kernels. The four bf16 and fp16 conversions in
  kernels/sircl_common.cuh are b12x's CuTe intrinsics from b12x/comm/roce/_cute_intrinsics.py (the
  copy in the SparkRing repository's third_party/b12x_roce, upstream base commit
  ffb7442d04a9f50b950df1fb17280acad881b7d5), written as CUDA inline PTX. SIRCL's one-shot and all-gather
  kernels, device intrinsics and progress-thread protocol derive from RoCEnante, the b12x one-shot
  RoCE collectives by Local Inference Lab and its contributors (https://github.com/local-inference-lab,
  b12x commit 236ddff04a5f5064084b46464800b70b34ec7d8c), licensed under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0. vendor/SIRCL-NOTICE reproduces SIRCL's NOTICE; SOURCE_SNAPSHOT.json records the
  SIRCL files this library follows.

libibverbs header code
  The RDMA transport is compiled against <infiniband/verbs.h> from rdma-core and contains code from
  that header's inline functions, used under the OpenIB.org BSD license. The copyright notices,
  conditions and disclaimer are in LICENSES/rdma-core-verbs.txt.

CUDA
  The library's build compiles its kernel packs (kernels/*.cu) with the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit's
  nvcc and embeds them in the library. The packs contain object code generated from CUDA Toolkit
  headers; in a built library that object code is distributed under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit End
  User License Agreement (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/) and is not licensed under the
  Apache License. See LICENSES/CUDA-NOTICE.txt.

